{"title":"Resources","slug":"Resources","html":"<p>This page maintains a list of resources related to operating system development. Often, links become outdated or sites go down. If a link does not work, try to see if it was backed up on archive.org.</p>\n<h2 id=\"operating_system_development\">Operating System Development</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.osdever.net/\" rel=\"noopener\">Bonafide OS Development</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles\" rel=\"noopener\">The Operating System Resource Center</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.acm.uiuc.edu/sigops/roll_your_own/\" rel=\"noopener\">How to Write an Operating System</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://www.devimperium.com/tutorials/start_your_small_operating_system_in_assembly\" rel=\"noopener\">Start your small Operating System in Assembly</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://neuraldk.org/writing.php?FilterCat=Os+Development&amp;FilterDev=All\" rel=\"noopener\">NeuralDK OSDev Tuts</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.brokenthorn.com/Resources/OSDevIndex.html\" rel=\"noopener\">BrokenThorn OS Development Tutorials</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/MiscellaneousSoftware/\" rel=\"noopener\">OS FAQ, overall design, VM design, threads..</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/MemoryManagement/\" rel=\"noopener\">Memory Management</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/ProtectedMode/\" rel=\"noopener\">Protected Mode</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.dtweed.com/circuitcellar/\" rel=\"noopener\">Circuit Cellar Ink, an embedded systems development magazine</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://createyourownos.blogspot.com/\" rel=\"noopener\">Create Your Own OS (by Pritam Zope)</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://github.com/dreamos82/Osdev-Notes\" rel=\"noopener\">Osdev Notes - A set of notes on how to write an operating system</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"hardware_specifications\">Hardware Specifications</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://perso.wanadoo.fr/pierrelib/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\">Pierre's Library</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.mcamafia.de/pdf/pdfref.htm\" rel=\"noopener\">List of PS/2 documents</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://datasheets.chipdb.org/\" rel=\"noopener\">ChipDB datasheet archive</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160313204854/https://freemicronix.org/docs/\" rel=\"noopener\">FreeMicroNix Documentation Collection</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"processors\">Processors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://software.intel.com/en-us/articles/intel-sdm/\" rel=\"noopener\">Intel Manuals</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/ProcessorArchitecture/\" rel=\"noopener\">Processor Architecture</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://developer.amd.com/resources/developer-guides-manuals/\" rel=\"noopener\">x86-64(AMD64)</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"bios\">BIOS</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20100102024125/http://phoenix.com/NR/rdonlyres/56E38DE2-3E6F-4743-835F-B4A53726ABED/0/specsbbs101.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">BIOS Boot Specification</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20180202045759/http://download.intel.com/support/motherboards/desktop/sb/pnpbiosspecificationv10a.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">Plug and Play BIOS Specification</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"motherboard_devices\">Motherboard Devices</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/MiscellaneousDevices/\" rel=\"noopener\">PIC, PIT, DMA, RTC, ..</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"human_input_devices\">Human Input Devices</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/pc16550d.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">Serial Mouse</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/HumanInterfaceDevices/\" rel=\"noopener\">Human Interface Devices</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Topic:8323\" rel=\"noopener\">PS/2 mice</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Topic:10247\" rel=\"noopener\">PS2 mouse driver</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"video\">Video</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.vesa.org\" rel=\"noopener\">official VESA &amp; VBE website</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"storage\">Storage</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.t13.org\" rel=\"noopener\">official ATA working group</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.ata-atapi.com/\" rel=\"noopener\">another ATA/ATAPI website, includes reference driver</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20091027131605/http://geocities.com/SiliconValley/2072/atapi.htm\" rel=\"noopener\">an introduction to ATA/ATAPI commands</a>. It contains a couple of ASM examples to read sectors and identify drives.</li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/DiskandDiscDrives/\" rel=\"noopener\">Disk and Disc Drives</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Topic:8339\" rel=\"noopener\">collected links about Ultra DMA, on ATA drives and how PCI configuration comes.</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"audio\">Audio</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/SoundDevices/\" rel=\"noopener\">Sound Devices</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"network_and_communication_ports\">Network and Communication ports</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/CommunicationDevices/\" rel=\"noopener\">Serial and Parallel port, SPP, EPP, ECP</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/NetworkingDevices/\" rel=\"noopener\">Networking Devices</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://pdf1.alldatasheet.com/datasheet-pdf/view/84677/ETC/RTL8139/+5_5J8UCRC/1SuMCAY.+/datasheet.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">RTL8139 family datasheet</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"buses\">Buses</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/InterconnectBuses/\" rel=\"noopener\">Interconnect Buses</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.usb.org/developers/docs\" rel=\"noopener\">official USB developers docs</a>z</li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://retired.beyondlogic.org/usb/usbdevdrvs.htm\" rel=\"noopener\">more USB info</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.o3one.org/hwdocs/usb/hcir1_0a.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">USB OHCI</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://www.intel.com/content/dam/www/public/us/en/documents/technical-specifications/ehci-specification-for-usb.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">USB EHCI</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://download.microsoft.com/download/1/6/1/161ba512-40e2-4cc9-843a-923143f3456c/ohci_11.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">OHCI for FireWire</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.o3one.org/hwdocs/usb/hcir1_0a.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">OHCI mirror</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"software_specifications\">Software Specifications</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.delorie.com/djgpp/doc/rbinter/ix/\" rel=\"noopener\">Ralf Brown's Interrupt List</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/TheBootProcess/\" rel=\"noopener\">The Boot Process</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/Partitions/\" rel=\"noopener\">Partitions</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/FileSystems/\" rel=\"noopener\">File Systems</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/ExecutableFileFormats/\" rel=\"noopener\">Executable File Formats</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/PlugandPlaySpecs/\" rel=\"noopener\">Plug'n'Play Specs</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/DeviceDriverInterfaces/\" rel=\"noopener\">Device Driver Interfaces</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://home.teleport.com/~brainy/fatgen102.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">FAT12-32</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Art-Software-Security-Assessment-Vulnerabilities/dp/0321444426\" rel=\"noopener\">The Art of Software Security Assessment</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Hacking-Art-Exploitation-Jon-Erickson/dp/1593271441/ref=pd_bbs_sr_1?ie=UTF8&amp;s=books&amp;qid=1210492590&amp;sr=1-1\" rel=\"noopener\">Art of Exploitation</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Reversing-Secrets-Engineering-Eldad-Eilam/dp/0764574817/ref=pd_bbs_sr_1?ie=UTF8&amp;s=books&amp;qid=1210492638&amp;sr=1-1\" rel=\"noopener\">Secrets of Reverse Engineering</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Rootkits-Subverting-Addison-Wesley-Software-Security/dp/0321294319/ref=pd_bbs_3?ie=UTF8&amp;s=books&amp;qid=1210492638&amp;sr=1-3\" rel=\"noopener\">Subverting the Windows Kernel</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"other_specifications\">Other Specifications</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://alexfru.narod.ru/emiscdocs.html\" rel=\"noopener\">stockpile of technical documents (partly in Russian)</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130119090155/http://www.nondot.org/sabre/os/articles/OtherHardware/\" rel=\"noopener\">Legos, ATX, NetPC's..</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"source_code\">Source Code</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://files.osdev.org/mirrors/geezer/osd/snippets.htm\" rel=\"noopener\">OSD Code Snippet Index</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.singlix.org/trdos/specs.html\" rel=\"noopener\">stockpile of documents at singlix.org</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://gee.cs.oswego.edu/pub/misc/malloc.c\" rel=\"noopener\">a reference implementation for malloc()</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"university_courses\">University Courses</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20090507122053/http://www.scs.cs.nyu.edu/aos/\" rel=\"noopener\">Advanced Operating Systems (NYU)</a></li>\n<li>Operating System Engineering (MIT) <a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://pdos.csail.mit.edu/6.828/2004/\" rel=\"noopener\">(2004)</a> <a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://ocw.mit.edu/OcwWeb/Electrical-Engineering-and-Computer-Science/6-828Fall-2006/CourseHome/index.htm\" rel=\"noopener\">(2006)</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~solomon/cs537.html\" rel=\"noopener\">Introduction to Operating Systems (WISC)</a></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"operating_system_development","text":"Operating System Development","level":2},{"id":"hardware_specifications","text":"Hardware Specifications","level":2},{"id":"processors","text":"Processors","level":3},{"id":"bios","text":"BIOS","level":3},{"id":"motherboard_devices","text":"Motherboard Devices","level":3},{"id":"human_input_devices","text":"Human Input Devices","level":3},{"id":"video","text":"Video","level":3},{"id":"storage","text":"Storage","level":3},{"id":"audio","text":"Audio","level":3},{"id":"network_and_communication_ports","text":"Network and Communication ports","level":3},{"id":"buses","text":"Buses","level":3},{"id":"software_specifications","text":"Software Specifications","level":2},{"id":"other_specifications","text":"Other Specifications","level":2},{"id":"source_code","text":"Source Code","level":2},{"id":"university_courses","text":"University Courses","level":2}],"categories":["Resources"],"rating":null,"flags":[],"words":331,"summary":"This page maintains a list of resources related to operating system development. Often, links become outdated or sites go down. If a link does not work, try to see if it was backed up on archive.org.","updated":"2023-08-20","authors":["Finarfin"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/Resources","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=Resources&action=history","backlinks":[{"t":"Getting Started","s":"Getting_Started"},{"t":"Security","s":"Security"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"Troubleshooting"}],"lessons":[{"id":"t1m1l2","title":"Prerequisite self-check","kind":"further"}]}